sequenceDiagram
  %% Target design: ADR 0244 task, one Swamp run with the shared route reconcile child (route.reconcile). docs/reference/routes.md#change-a-tld-cluster-state-or-cluster-membership.
  %% status: draft
  %% command: cluster:node:add
  %% kind: cluster.node_add
  autonumber
  %% lane CLI icon=terminal pill=caller tone=gray
  %% lane GW icon=gateway pill=intent tone=blue
  %% lane SW icon=workflow pill=executes tone=green
  %% lane N icon=server pill=target tone=amber
  %% lane V icon=server pill=target tone=purple
  participant CLI as CLI / MCP<br/>orbit · MCP tools
  participant GW as Gateway<br/>Laravel API
  participant SW as Swamp<br/>workflow execution
  participant N as Cluster Nodes<br/>Router · members
  participant V as DNS targets<br/>resolvers · peers
  CLI->>GW: cluster:node:add<br/>CLUSTER NODE
  Note over GW: Validate, lock, plan<br/>transitions stored
  %%> Requirements:
  %%> - the calling Node has an access grant to the Node being attached
  %%> - the Node is active (`cluster.node_inactive`), belongs to no other Cluster (`cluster.membership_conflict`), and its LAN address is free in the Cluster (`cluster.lan_ip_conflict`); a Route that would take Cluster scope needs an active Router (`route.router_required`)
  %%> - every affected Route keeps a valid domain, scope and target; one refusal leaves every Route in place; an active public Route that the change would move is refused (`route.reconciliation_required`)
  %%> - no other Cluster change runs; the Gateway waits up to 30 seconds, then refuses with `cluster.router_busy`
  %%> Stored:
  %%> - the Node stays outside the Cluster with a pending membership; a pending replacement is stored for each domain change and the old placement for each scope change
  alt Cluster is active, or the Node is already a member
    GW->>SW: Start run, full intent<br/>operation-cluster-node-add
    GW-->>CLI: 202 Accepted<br/>task ID
    SW->>N: Open LAN ingress<br/>@swamp/cfgmgmt/firewall
    %%> Why first:
    %%> - the Router opens HTTPS and DNS to the member's LAN address before private DNS sends the member there; identical lines stay
    %%> Without a LAN address:
    %%> - the member gets no LAN rule and is reached over WireGuard
    opt Routes change
      SW->>N: Reconcile the Routes<br/>child route-reconcile
      %%> What it does:
      %%> - moves the Node's Routes to the Cluster scope, with generated domains in the Cluster TLD when it has one; custom proxy Routes keep their Node scope; the cutover is inside the child
    end
    SW->>V: Select the Router in DNS<br/>child dns-publish
    %%> DNS answers:
    %%> - the vpn Node answers WireGuard addresses; the Cluster Router resolver answers its LAN members with LAN addresses through a DNS delegate
    %%> DNS lifecycle:
    %%> - the shared publication checks the VPN and Cluster projections, moves affected Cluster DNS delegates and VPN policies, and holds old resolver cleanup until every member confirms (ADR 0248)
    SW->>N: Prune unused rules<br/>@swamp/cfgmgmt/firewall absent
    %%> Why it always runs:
    %%> - after a failure before the cutover it removes the LAN rules and DNS selection the stored state does not need
    alt every step succeeds
      SW-->>GW: Run succeeded<br/>terminal event
      Note over GW: Record the membership<br/>Routes cut over
      %%> When:
      %%> - at the cutover when Routes change, and when the run succeeds when none do
    else a step fails
      SW--xGW: Run failed<br/>error_code, failed step
      Note over GW: Read the failed step<br/>cutover or not
      %%> Result before the cutover:
      %%> - the Node stays outside the Cluster and every Route keeps its domain and scope
      %%> Result after the cutover:
      %%> - the Node is a member; a rerun finishes the withdrawal, the DNS selection and the prune
      %%> Retry:
      %%> - run the same command again; every step runs again and skips what already matches
    end
    loop every 2 s until terminal
      CLI->>GW: operation:show TASK
      GW-->>CLI: status + result
    end
  else Cluster is inactive and the Node is not a member
    GW-->>CLI: 200 OK<br/>Node attached
    %%> Result:
    %%> - the membership is recorded at once; no Node is contacted and no traffic changes
  end
